# vehje-runtime-abi, known gaps

## no-std

The crate root carries `#![cfg_attr(not(feature = "std"), no_std)]`
with `default = ["std"]` rather than a hardcoded `#![no_std]`. The
`std` cargo feature is on by default for stable cdylib builds: a
cdylib on stable Rust requires a panic runtime, which std provides
out of the box. Disabling the std feature switches to the gated
`#[panic_handler]` in `lib.rs` for embedded targets that bring their
own unwind story. The lint pack reads only the literal `#![no_std]`
and does not yet recognise the cfg_attr form; refining the lint to
treat the cfg_attr pattern as compliant is parked under a future
mockspace task. Until then this gap is documented and accepted.
